==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Fallen Bear]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 93.33~96.67 seconds<sup>2,800f~2,900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>, delay 83.33~90 seconds<sup>2,500f~2,700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 240 seconds<sup>7,200f</sup>, delay 83.33~90 seconds<sup>2,500f~2,700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**5 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
**1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Since the difficulty of the stage is determined not just by your units, but also by luck of [[Surge Attack#Death Surge|Death Surge]]/Jagando Surges not spawning on your main attackers and your [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]], you aren't always guaranteed to win this stage. However, [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|units with Surge Immunity]]/100% Shield Piercing will work better than others, as you won't need to rely too much on luck using them.

Before tackling this stage, ensure that you at least have these four units in your line-up; [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] (non-[[True Form]] so his speed is equal to Manic Eraser), [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]], as well as the [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] [[Battle Items]]. It is recommended to have your units to Lv.50, since Manic Eraser just barely survives Jagando's Surges while Lv50 Manic King Dragon barely survives a hit/Surge from Fallen Bear.

Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]], [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]] or [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]] can speed up the end of the stage where you are left slowly chipping away at Jagando until he dies after the support is exhausted. Alternatively, a Defense combo works just as well, as it gives Manic Eraser enough health to tank a hit from Fallen Bear.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] - Can be very useful in stalling Jagando especially if aided by Research Combos. Its massive health, immunities (meaning Condemned Peng can't slow it), high speed and relatively low cost can allow it to reliably delay Jagando by forcing him into attacking, whilst preventing the Surge from spawning if timed well. It also gives your other units (particularly Shield Piercers) a much better shot on the Fallen Bears by destroying any Cerberus Kids that happen to be obstructive. When the support dies out, it alone can practically pin Jagando indefinitely.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] - His 100% Shield Piercing and Knockback versus Traited enemies makes it a great choice against Jagando and Fallen Bear, although timing is required for it to actually get a hit in. A Lv.46+ Supercar Cat can actually kill a Fallen Bear in two hits. This can be very helpful as it will make it easier to stall Jagando and the Condemned Pengs.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]] (Lv49+) - Can be used to knockback Condemned Peng in one hit assuming Brave Cutter is active and they've [[Strengthen|Strengthened]] after surviving a lethal strike. However, due to Condemned Peng's 50% slow chance as well as Jagando's constant attacks, you have to time it very well.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] - In True Form, Cat Researcher boasts very high speed, rapid attacks and a 15% chance to destroy shields. Despite his Single Attacks, he is fairly easy to time, making him a simple but effective solution to any Shield, especially when fighting Fallen Bears.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] (Lv.46+) - Can also be used to deal enough damage to knockback Condemned Peng in one hit. Not only that, but if it lands the killing blow, it can provide you with a cash boost well exceeding its summon cost. Just hope that they don't get slowed or sniped before they get there.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Can be used to take 2 knockbacks from an exposed Fallen Bear, skipping one Shield regeneration, and giving Bullet Train a chance to finish him once the final shield goes down. Bahamut can also be used during the final part of the stage to chip Jagando and take out the Condemned Pengs. He requires precise timing though, as Fallen Bear will always destroy him in a single hit.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] - Essentially trivializes the stage if you could afford the extreme evolution cost. Being [[Strong Against|strong against]] [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]], [[Immune to Surge|Immune to Surges]] and with decent stats against them, it holds the threats rather well with its singular knockback. They can even survive two hits from Fallen Bear at level 48 or above.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]] - Similar to Cat Cactus, this unit completely trivializes this stage. Despite not having [[Immune to Surge|Immune to Surges]], it is [[Resistant|resistant against]] [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] which helps it tank all the surges from the enemies. However, you have to beat an [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|incredibly difficult stage]] before getting it. You can use Maize as a solo [[Meatshield class Cats|meatshield]] if you bring research combos equivalent to 1 M Research Combo.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] - If you are lucky enough to have it, Brainwashed Cat would be a amazing meatshield to use for this stage due to being spammable and having a 30% to dodge attacks from every enemy in the stage.
*[[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] - A extremely good attacker when you invest in their Surge Immunity and Mini-wave, if you bring a Rich Cat you can comfortably spawn them occasionally to deal with the Condemned Pengs and Fallen Bear, along with sometimes getting a lucky hit on Jagando.
*[[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] - Similar to Li'l King Dragon, can function as a budget version of them when you need to save for a more expensive unit. He is very fragile, meaning any moderately powerful blow will take him out. However, his Resistant Talent flips this on its head, raising his effective health high enough to tank both Jagando's final hit and the Surge it spawns. Being able to bounce back after Jagando's attacks gives him many more opportunities to hit.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] - Can be used to knock back Jagando, Fallen Bear, and Condemned Peng. Sniper basically trivializes this stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]] - An [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] [[Long Distance]] crowd-control specialist with Surge Immunity, Satoru is able to slow Aku threats and has a 20% chance to destroy their Shields. In True Form, he only gets better with 100% chance to cause [[Knockback|knockback]] and 50% chance to destroy Shields. He deals with Fallen Bears very well. He also outranges Jagando's Onmistrike by 30 range.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]] - Kai is admittedly only useful with her True Form unlocked and her Shield Piercing Talent fully upgraded, as that's when her disposability and bulk for a tank comes into use. At Lv.39 or above, Kai can nuke a Fallen Bear in a single attack if her hit connects, allowing the player to focus on stalling Jagando and killing Condemned Pengs until the next Fallen Bear spawns during which Kai's fast recharge allows you to replace her easily. Even higher level Kais can also survive the initial encounter and break Jagando's shield too, making the rest of the fight easier. Just make sure Cerberus Kids, Condemned Pengs, or Jagando himself don't block Kai's path to the Fallen Bears and cause her to waste her attack, otherwise she will likely die before getting a second chance.
*[[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]] - Hevijak has 50% Shield Piercing, knockback and [[Resistant|resistance]] vs. Aku enemies. While he cannot outrange Jagando's Omni Strike, Hevijak can avoid his attacks while dealing with the Condemned Pengs and Fallen Bears. His resistance to Aku enemies allow him to tank their Surges. His knockback ability can also recover lost ground if it hits and activates, especially in his True Form with the 100% knockback chance. However, due to his slow attack rate, he works best when backed by other Shield Piercing units to ensure he actually knocks back the main threats.
*[[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Lilin π]] - Lilin is strong against Aku, with 100% chance to destroy Shields and generate [[Surge Attacks]]. She can just barely outrange Fallen Bear, and her Surge can also snipe enemies she may be unable to hit directly, specifically Jagando. Her short recharge also helps, allowing her to be easily replaced even if lost.
*[[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)|Malevolent Mad-Duck]] - Malevolent Mad-Duck boasts massive stats and Surge Immunity at a high range. Given all threats are within his target traits, he can put his sheer strength to good use. He won't be able to outrange Jagando and still can't get around Shields, but he's able to cripple Fallen Bears and can even land hits on Jagando too.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - with [[Massive Damage]] to Traited enemies, Surge Immunity, and 600 range plus Long Distance attacks, Phonoa stands out as a near perfect option for this stage. While they can't Pierce Shields, they can still deal significant damage. However, Phonoa is frail and requires a robust frontline to ensure threats can't enter their blindspot.
*[[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]] - Diabolosa boasts Massive Damage against Aku through relatively rapid attacks, being able to outrange Jagando's Omni Strike by 25, and can gain Surge Immunity through Talents. It also possesses the efficient [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] Combo with [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying]], which increases unit damage by 15% for just two slots.
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]] - Massive Damage against Aku, an Omni Strike range of -100~400, while also having a guaranteed Shield Piercing makes him a good unit for gradually chipping away at Lord of Ruin Jagando or Fallen Bear since his high speed will usually ensure he lands at least a hit or two. At a high enough level, he can even eliminate Fallen Bear in 2-3 hits.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]] – A powerhouse with 100% Shield Piercing as well as Massive Damage/Resistance to Aku and Slow Immunity, Hanayama is able to tank and dish out extreme amounts of damage while bypassing Shields. His singular knockback actually helps him in this regard since all enemies here are within his targeted trait. Despite his long foreswing and overall attack cycle that can lead to him wasting an attack on peons, his use shouldn't be discounted.
*[[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Lucifer]] – Being a surge immune sniper who outranges every enemy in this stage and is strong against aku, Lucifer is the perfect option for this stage, dishing out consistent dps from a safe distance with little to no issue. His guaranteed surges act as additional dps and wall out weaker peons.

